From: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ufs: ufs-qcom: Balance repeated lane clock enables

The Hibern8 setup-clocks callback and the UFS device resume callback
both request the Qualcomm lane clocks. Each call increments the clock
framework's prepare and enable counts, while suspend disables the
clocks once using the shared is_lane_clks_enabled flag.

On SM8750 the three symbol clock branch enable counts each increased
from 55 to 60 across six consecutive runtime-suspended samples. Each
sample followed a direct storage read and a return to runtime suspend.
The outstanding references keep the symbol muxes from parking at XO.

Use the existing flag to make the enable operation idempotent, as the
disable operation already is. The first enable and its error handling
retain the existing clock sequence.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-scsi/20250909055149.2068737-1-quic_pkambar@quicinc.com/
Signed-off-by: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index c0d452dc4aebfc691948af456d575d89802acedd..1c74c2639699ea3ee1795fcd8998de0ba484ac90 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 {
 	int err;
 
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
